"""engine v2: the declared hand bases of the committed duty sheets - the
composer lane's data half (flow_graph/v2/render/duties.py composes them).

House doctrine (AGENTS.md, repository roles): generated artifacts are never
hand-edited; they regenerate from the model. This module is the complement,
not an exception: it holds no generated bytes at all. Each value is the
AUTHORED engineering prose of one committed duty sheet, captured verbatim at
migration time - the page's hand and historical text (the frozen `Graph Rev`
header line, per-unit sections 4, 5 and 8, hand-rewritten envelope tails,
manufacturing-pointer variants, converged section 3 lines, whole hand
sections 2) - with every generator-owned fragment span replaced by its
declared anchor. The bases are declared data: they never regenerate, they
are never hand-edited by the pipeline, and the only thing that ever rewrites
one is a human author revising the page (the same act that edits any hand
document). The generated fragments themselves render fresh from the model at
composition time (duties.render_*), so the module cannot go stale against
the graph: a graph change moves a fragment, and the composition moves with
it; a hand revision moves a base, and the registry's byte-exact gate sees it.

An anchor is the placeholder span `{{AQS-FRAG:<fragment id>}}` set into the
line or section span the fragment owns (section 2 span anchors carry the
trailing blank line; the envelope anchor carries the idiom's `m³.` stamp
shape), crafted to match the v1 patch idiom's own regex. The composition is
therefore the v1 patch operation applied to the declared base: replace the
unique anchor with the fresh fragment bytes. Pure string data: no imports,
no I/O, no float literals (the numbers inside the prose are string bytes).
"""

